-- ind-b-tests-ambiguous: the assertions of test author ind-b that do not hold on the encoding where the SOURCE is ambiguous: each asserts the reading ind-b
-- took in work/ind-b/expectations.md (section "Ambiguous rows"), and the encoding takes the other.  Each was moved here unedited when it failed.
-- EXPECTED: 2 failed assertions.  A-10 was decided before opening the encoding; A-14 was added after (see expectations.md, last section).

§ `Ambiguities with G7 (Part 6)`

-- A-10 (reading A, taken): an unregistered Jersey entity that calls itself a "Jersey charity" also refers to itself as a "charity": contravenes 21(3) as well as 23(1).
-- Reading B (the encoding's): only 23(1) is contravened, because "Jersey charity" is the expression Article 23 regulates.
#ASSERT `Art 21(3) the statement contravenes paragraph (3)` `ind-b7 a Jersey company` FALSE (`ind-b7 the entity says it is` `ind-b7 Jersey charity` TRUE)

§ `Ambiguities with G2 (Article 7)`

-- A-14 (reading A, taken weakly; added after opening): an entity that benefits only one named natural person does not provide public benefit, whoever determines
-- the question.  Reading B (the encoding's): Article 7(1) applies 7(3)(b) only to the Commissioner, the tribunal and the court, so a finding by anyone else stands.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 7 the entity provides public benefit` `ind-b A` (`ind-b entity` `ind-b general` (LIST `ind-b education`)) (`ind-b determination of an entity benefiting only identified persons, by` `any person` TRUE)
